Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:02.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if the Moon disappeared?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.57,0:00:04.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Without a sound.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.74,0:00:06.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You step outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.20,0:00:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You look up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.31,0:00:08.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The sky is empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.74,0:00:10.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Just stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.87,0:00:12.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.59,0:00:13.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.93,0:00:16.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every night is now pitch black.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.39,0:00:17.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No more moonlight.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.82,0:00:19.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.62,0:00:21.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.02,0:00:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The oceans feel it first.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.86,0:00:25.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The tides shrink to about one third.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.22,0:00:28.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Coastlines go strangely still.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.62,0:00:29.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one month.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.97,0:00:33.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Corals that spawn by the full moon lose their signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.88,0:00:36.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Night hunters lose their light.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.59,0:00:38.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After millions of years.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.45,0:00:43.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Without the Moon holding it steady, Earth's tilt could start to wobble.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.41,0:00:45.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The seasons could go wild.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.20,0:00:47.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.93,0:00:50.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The Moon is already leaving us.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.10,0:00:53.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In nineteen sixty-nine, astronauts left mirrors on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.95,0:00:56.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Scientists still fire lasers at them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.48,0:01:01.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Every year, the Moon drifts about three point eight centimeters away.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.36,0:01:02.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.50,0:01:05.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Next time you see the Moon… look up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.13,0:01:07.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It won't stay this close forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.46,0:01:08.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Would you miss it?
